@adamdotdevin  @Hona  All issues regarding memory leaks have been addressed so far, so this pr is almost irrelevant now, just 2 more things remain in the diff to dev: 
 1. Memory leak — cleanup callback for FileTime.state (clears read map + locks on disposal)                                                                                                                                                                           
 2. Windows mtime — uses filesystem mtime instead of new Date() to avoid NTFS clock divergence ; 
 
Let me know if this is relevant or I should close it. (thanks for fixing all those memory leaks :D )

@rekram1-node This PR is being blocked by a known flaky E2E test (issue #14461). The test failures are unrelated to my changes which only fix the textarea collapsing issue (PR #15073). 

Since this is a test infrastructure issue affecting multiple contributors, could this PR be allowed to merge despite the transient test failures? The core functionality change is solid and has been tested locally.

If needed, I'm happy to help investigate the flaky test, but this appears to be a pre-existing race condition in project switching tests.

